<title>USA: Sony, Ogden to co-produce films.</title>
<headline>Sony, Ogden to co-produce films.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Corp and Ogden Corp have signed a co-production agreement to make large format films, the Japanese entertainment company said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Sony said the three-year agreement would cover the financing, development and production for projects from both Sony and Ogden's entertainment division.</p>
<p>It did not reveal the financial terms of the agreement.</p>
<p>Sony Pictures Classics, a division of Sony Pictures Entertainment, will handle global marketing and distribution of the films, which will fall in the &quot;broad family and education genre in an entertaining format,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The first film under the agreement would be &quot;Mark Twain's America,&quot; to be produced and directed by Stephen Low.</p>
</text>
